IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART VI, "Alternate Access to Special Benefits": reg 93.
-- Text: the plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (SOR-96-332.txt, lines 1709-1722);
-- an unofficial conversion, not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT IT DOES. A person who has too few hours for benefits under section 7 of the Act but has had an interruption of earnings
-- and 600 or more hours qualifies for SPECIAL benefits (sickness, maternity, parental, compassionate care, family caregiver);
-- those benefits are then paid under ss 22 to 23.3 of the Act with a substituted proof for each working day (reg 93(4));
-- and, if they later accumulate enough hours, regular benefits become payable (reg 93(5)).
--
-- WHAT IS TAKEN AS AN INPUT, AND WHY. Section 7 (who qualifies), section 9, section 18 (availability for work), ss 22 to 23.3,
-- the table to s 7(2) and the meaning of a week of unemployment are piece ei1's; the interruption of earnings (reg 14) is piece
-- er1's; the illness, injury and quarantine of reg 40(4) and (5) are piece er3's. Each is a plain input with a comment
-- "out of range" that names the section and the piece. The day on which subsection 93(4.1) "comes into force" is not in the text
-- (the converter drops the historical notes that carry it): it is an input.
--
-- Hohfeld, for the Jural relations table in NOTES.md: reg 93(1) and (2) give the insured person a claim (to qualify, to have a
-- benefit period established) against the Commission, which is bound; reg 93(4) puts on the claimant the liability to be refused
-- payment for a working day they cannot prove; reg 93(5) gives a conditional claim to regular benefits.

§ `Part VI -- Alternate Access to Special Benefits`

§§ `reg 93(1) who qualifies`

-- src:1710 | 93 (1) An insured person who does not qualify to receive benefits under section 7 of the Act and who is claiming special benefits qualifies to receive the special benefits if the person
-- src:1711 | (a) has had an interruption of earnings from employment; and
-- src:1712 | (b) has had 600 or more hours of insurable employment in their qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(1) (src:1710-1712)
GIVEN `is employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has been employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `qualifies to receive benefits under section 7 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 7 (piece ei1)
      `the reason for the benefits claimed` IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `has had an interruption of earnings from employment` IS A BOOLEAN        -- out of range: reg 14 (piece er1)
      `hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(1) the insured person qualifies to receive special benefits under this regulation` IF
        `s 2(1) insured person` `is employed in insurable employment` `has been employed in insurable employment`
    AND NOT (`qualifies to receive benefits under section 7 of the Act`)
    AND `s 2(1) special benefits` `the reason for the benefits claimed`
    AND `has had an interruption of earnings from employment`
    AND `hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` AT LEAST 600

§§ `reg 93(2) the benefit period, and the weeks for which benefits are payable`

-- src:1713 | (2) Notwithstanding section 9 of the Act, where an insured person who qualifies under subsection (1) to receive special benefits makes an initial claim for benefits, a benefit period shall be established in respect of the person and, once it is established, special benefits are payable to the person in accordance with this section for each week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(2), first limb: "a benefit period shall be established" (src:1713)
GIVEN `the insured person qualifies under subsection (1) to receive special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insured person makes an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(2) a benefit period is established for the insured person notwithstanding section 9 of the Act` IF
        `the insured person qualifies under subsection (1) to receive special benefits`
    AND `the insured person makes an initial claim for benefits`

-- "a week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period": a week falls in the benefit period when the whole week lies in it
-- (fork F-WEEK-FALLS in NOTES.md; benefit periods begin on a Sunday, so the readings agree on a benefit period of whole weeks).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(2), second limb: "special benefits are payable ... for each week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period" (src:1713)
GIVEN `a benefit period has been established for the insured person under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 11 of the Act (piece ei1)
      `the week` IS A `Period of days`
      `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(2) special benefits are payable for the week` IF
        `a benefit period has been established for the insured person under subsection (2)`
    AND `it is a week of unemployment`
    AND `the day` (`the week`'s `first day of the period`) `falls within` `the benefit period`
    AND `the day` (`the week`'s `last day of the period`) `falls within` `the benefit period`

§§ `reg 93(3) ss 22 to 23.3 of the Act apply`

-- The text says "sections 22 to 23.3"; reg 93(4)(b) lists the sections in that range as 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 and 23.3.
-- "Subject to subsection (4)": subsection (4) replaces the proof of availability that s 18 asks for.
-- src:1714 | (3) Subject to subsection (4), sections 22 to 23.3 of the Act apply to the payment of special benefits under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(3) (src:1714)
GIVEN `the insured person qualifies under subsection (1) to receive special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section of the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(3) the section of the Act applies to the payment of special benefits under this regulation` IF
        `the insured person qualifies under subsection (1) to receive special benefits`
    AND elem `the section of the Act` (LIST 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2, 23.3)

§§ `reg 93(4) and (4.1) payment for a working day`

-- src:1718 | (4.1) A claimant to whom benefits are payable under any of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act and whose claim for benefits because of illness, injury or quarantine is made for a week that begins on or after the day on which this subsection comes into force is not disentitled under paragraph (4)(a) for failing to prove that they would have been available for work were it not for the illness, injury or quarantine.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(4.1), the day it comes into force (src:1718)
GIVEN `the first day of the week for which the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which subsection 93(4.1) comes into force` IS A DATE   -- not in the text: the converter drops the historical notes
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(4.1) the week begins on or after the day on which the subsection comes into force` IF
    `the first day of the week for which the claim is made` AT LEAST `the day on which subsection 93(4.1) comes into force`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(4.1) (src:1718)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant under one of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: ss 23 to 23.3 (piece ei1)
      `the claim is made because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week begins on or after the day on which this subsection comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(4.1) the claimant is not disentitled under paragraph (4)(a) for failing to prove availability for work` IF
        `benefits are payable to the claimant under one of sections 23 to 23.3 of the Act`
    AND `the claim is made because of illness, injury or quarantine`
    AND `the week begins on or after the day on which this subsection comes into force`

-- "a claimant is not entitled to be paid special benefits for a working day ... in respect of which the claimant fails to prove that
-- on that day the claimant was (a) ... or (b) ...". So the claimant is not refused for the day when they prove (a) or prove (b);
-- the subsection says nothing about when payment is due, only when it is refused for want of proof.
-- src:1715 | (4) Notwithstanding section 18 of the Act, a claimant is not entitled to be paid special benefits for a working day, in a benefit period established under this section, in respect of which the claimant fails to prove that on that day the claimant was
-- src:1716 | (a) unable to work because of an illness, injury or quarantine referred to in subsection 40(4) or (5) and that the claimant would otherwise be available for work; or
-- src:1717 | (b) entitled to benefits under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(4) (src:1715-1717)
GIVEN `the claimant proves that on that day they were unable to work because of an illness, injury or quarantine referred to in subsection 40(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 40(4) and (5) (piece er3)
      `the claimant proves that on that day they would otherwise be available for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 93(4.1) relieves the claimant of proving that` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proves that on that day they were entitled to benefits under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: ss 22 to 23.3 (piece ei1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(4) the claimant is not refused special benefits for the working day for want of proof` IF
        (    `the claimant proves that on that day they were unable to work because of an illness, injury or quarantine referred to in subsection 40(4) or (5)`
         AND (   `the claimant proves that on that day they would otherwise be available for work`
              OR `subsection 93(4.1) relieves the claimant of proving that`))
    OR  `the claimant proves that on that day they were entitled to benefits under section 22, 23, 23.1, 23.2 or 23.3 of the Act`

§§ `reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits`

-- src:1719 | (5) Subject to section 18 of the Act, regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for a week of unemployment to a claimant who has received special benefits under this section where
-- src:1720 | (a) the claimant has accumulated, since the beginning of their benefit period, a number of hours of insurable employment that, when added to the number of those hours in their qualifying period, equal or exceed the number of hours set out in the table to subsection 7(2) of the Act in relation to the regional rate of unemployment that was applicable to the claimant at the beginning of their benefit period; and
-- src:1721 | (b) any regular benefits or additional special benefits are payable to the claimant in that benefit period in accordance with the Act, based on the hours of insurable employment in the claimant's qualifying period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(5) (src:1719-1721)
GIVEN `the claimant has received special benefits under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours of insurable employment accumulated since the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER
      `hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours set out in the table to subsection 7(2) of the Act for the regional rate of unemployment that applied at the beginning of the benefit period` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: s 7(2) (piece ei1)
      `regular or additional special benefits are payable in the benefit period under the Act on the hours in the qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: Part I (piece ei1)
      `section 18 of the Act does not bar payment for the week` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 18 (piece ei1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(5) regular benefits and additional special benefits are payable for the week of unemployment` IF
        `section 18 of the Act does not bar payment for the week`
    AND `the claimant has received special benefits under this regulation`
    AND (`hours of insurable employment accumulated since the beginning of the benefit period` PLUS `hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period`)
            AT LEAST `the hours set out in the table to subsection 7(2) of the Act for the regional rate of unemployment that applied at the beginning of the benefit period`
    AND `regular or additional special benefits are payable in the benefit period under the Act on the hours in the qualifying period`

§§ `reg 93(6) everything else applies`

-- src:1722 | (6) Except as otherwise provided in this section, the provisions of the Act and these Regulations apply to claimants claiming benefits under this section.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 93(6) (src:1722)
GIVEN `the claimant is claiming benefits under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this regulation provides otherwise for the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(6) a provision of the Act or of the Regulations applies to the claimant` IF
        `the claimant is claiming benefits under this regulation`
    AND NOT (`this regulation provides otherwise for the provision`)
